{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model underpredicts the true path almost every day, typically by ~2–5 EUR, with the gap widening during rallies.",
    "Trend/lag error: when the market transitions from flat/down to a sustained uptrend, the forecast lags and fails to capture the slope; apply an upward trend adjustment when the last ~5–10 days show rising momentum.",
    "Volatility compression: forecast range is too narrow versus realized moves; increase amplitude (especially on upside) during trending regimes.",
    "Horizon-dependent drift: underprediction grows with lead time (later days are more biased low than early days); use a correction that increases with forecast horizon (e.g., additive ramp).",
    "Missed regime shift after local lows: following a drawdown to ~60–62, the model expects mean reversion/sideways but reality breaks higher; treat sharp dips as potential launch points and reduce mean-reversion strength in that context."
  ]
}
